wifi_hal_nl80211: single-phy -- let START_AP set each radio channel

Issue F: on a FEATURE_SINGLE_PHY device (one physical wiphy projected as
wifi0/wifi1/wifi2), wifi_hal_setRadioOperatingParameters() -> nl80211_update_wiphy()
issues a standalone NL80211_CMD_SET_WIPHY + NL80211_ATTR_WIPHY_FREQ channel-set per
logical radio. On Linux 7.0 that request returns -EINVAL for the 2nd/3rd radio once a
sibling radio AP on the same phy is already beaconing (captured by nlmon: radio0/2437
OK, radio1/5180 and radio2/6135 -> -EINVAL, each with its own correct per-VIF IFINDEX;
the message carries no MLO/EHT/tx-power/antenna attrs -- it is the channel op itself).
The subsequent START_AP then fails -ENETDOWN downstream, so only 2.4 GHz beacons.

The kernel is not the limitation: a clean host-hwsim test (one phy, two AP VIFs)
brings up tst0@2437 and tst1@5180 to AP-ENABLED concurrently on 7.0 -- because the
AP-start (NL80211_CMD_NEW_BEACON) path carries each VIF chandef (nl80211_fill_chandef)
and gets its own channel context. Only the *standalone* pre-START_AP channel-set fails
while a sibling AP is active (6.8 tolerated it; 7.0 rejects it).

Fix: under FEATURE_SINGLE_PHY, skip the standalone SET_WIPHY channel-set in
nl80211_update_wiphy() and let START_AP carry each radio channel. txpower is already
set above via wifi_drv_set_txpower(); the Exit path (retry-limit/QAM/offload and BSS
re-enable) still runs. Scoped to FEATURE_SINGLE_PHY, so real multi-radio hardware is
unaffected.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 wifi_hal_nl80211.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/wifi_hal_nl80211.c b/wifi_hal_nl80211.c
--- a/wifi_hal_nl80211.c
+++ b/wifi_hal_nl80211.c
@@ -8384,6 +8384,18 @@
     wifi_hal_dbg_print("%s:%d: update transmitPower:%d\n", __func__, __LINE__, radio->oper_param.transmitPower);
     wifi_drv_set_txpower(interface, radio->oper_param.transmitPower);
 
+#if defined(FEATURE_SINGLE_PHY)
+    /* Issue F (Linux 7.0): the standalone SET_WIPHY channel-set below returns
+     * -EINVAL once a sibling logical-radio AP on the same physical wiphy is already
+     * beaconing (nlmon: radio1/radio2 SET_WIPHY -> -EINVAL while radio0 is up). The
+     * AP-start (NEW_BEACON) path already carries each VIF's chandef and establishes
+     * its own channel context -- proven on 7.0: two APs on two channels on one phy
+     * come up via START_AP. So under FEATURE_SINGLE_PHY skip the pre-START_AP wiphy
+     * channel-set here and let START_AP set each radio channel. (6.8 tolerated the
+     * standalone set, so this only changes behaviour on 7.0.) */
+    goto Exit;
+#endif
+
     msg = nl80211_drv_cmd_msg(g_wifi_hal.nl80211_id, NULL, 0, NL80211_CMD_SET_WIPHY);
     if (msg == NULL) {
         return -1;
